    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d95">

                <pb facs="0224" n="112" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg112"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/1408</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Straus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1782</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-13">April 13, 1935</date>.<lb/>[Received April
                        24.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Embassy’s despatch No.
                    1253 of October 2, 1934,<anchor n="10" xml:id="d95-f1"/> and to the recent sale
                    of the Chinese Eastern Railway, I have <pb facs="0225" n="113" xml:id="pg113"/>
                    the honor to report, as a matter of record, that the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs, in reply to a written question by Deputy Susset, published a statement
                    on page 4153 of the <hi rendition="#italic">Journal Officiel</hi> of April 12,
                    1935, confirming that the French Government had intervened for the purpose of
                    protecting French private interests in the Chinese Eastern Railway.</p>
                <p>The Minister emphasised that “very explicit reserves had once more been conveyed
                    to the Soviet and Japanese Governments immediately following the definitive
                    conclusion of the arrangement relating to this enterprise”.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. Merle
                            Cochran</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">First Secretary of
                        Embassy</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
